ers call the race Likely Republican, though two put it closer as Lean Republican. Polling has been sparse and comes entirely from Democratic-leaning sponsors, but the two most recent surveys show a contest near even, well inside the district's normal margin.\n\nFlood holds clear financial advantages, with $1.2 million on hand, and enters as the favorite on fundamentals. Backemeyer's fundraising and the national party's decision to target the district signal genuine Democratic interest, aided by a favorable national environment. Prediction markets give Flood roughly a three-in-four chance of holding the seat, consistent with a narrow but real Republican edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1466, "margin": -6.26}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1237, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1206, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2177, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1689, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1196, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1777, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2315, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1394, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1156, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.114, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1142, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1121, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.173, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1374, "margin": -6.6}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1133, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.1024, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.1161, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.106, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.1138, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.2195, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.1349, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.1345, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "